  |  Assembler Plus Tools READ.ME File Notes       LINK-86 Notes |
  |								 |
  |	    							 |
  |	    							 |
  |	 5. LINK-86 can  now  report  three  additional  error	 |
  |	    messages.						 |
  |								 |
  |	    CLASS NOT FOUND  -  The  class name  specified  in	 |
  |	    the command line does not  exist  in  any  of  the	 |
  |         being linked.					 |
  |	    							 |
  |	    GROUP NOT FOUND  -  The group name  specified  in	 |
  |	    the command line does not exist  in  any  of  the	 |
  |	    files being linked.					 |
  |	    							 |
  |	    SEGMENT NOT FOUND  -  The segment name  specified	 |
  |	    in the command line does not exist in any  of the	 |
  |	    files being linked.					 |
  |								 |
  |					    			 |
  |                          RASM-86 NOTES			 |
  |         ===============================================	 |
  |	    							 |
  |	  * A new command line option switch  has been  added	 |
  |	    to the RASM-86 assembler.  The $NC switch directs	 |
  |	    RASM-86 not to convert  letters  to  upper  case.	 |
  |	    This  feature  supports  users  of   C   language	 |
  |	    software.						 |
  |								 |
  |       * RASM-86 now supports 8087 opcodes, if you include    |
  |         file 8087DEF.A86 in your program.   Refer to that	 |
  |         file for the names of the 8087 opcodes.		 |
  |								 |
  |	    							 |
  |                           SID-86 Notes			 |
  |         ===============================================	 |
  |								 |
  |	  * SID-86 does  not currently support  symbol  files	 |
  |	    for programs configured according  to the  LARGE,	 |
  |	    COMPACT, or MEDIUM memory models.			 |
  |								 |
  |	    To  reference symbols in a LARGE or MEDIUM  model	 |
  |	    program,    you  must  refer  to  the  .MAP  file	 |
  |	    generated for the program by LINK-86.    The .MAP	 |
  |	    file   provides   you   with   relative   segment	 |
  |       							 |
  |                             Page 2				 |
  |								 |
